# Secure Runtime Alpha 8121-8200 -- Reproducibility Finding 1 (external
# clean-checkout audit `73fc0b2`): on a Windows machine with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and no `.gitattributes`, every tracked text file is
# checked out with CRLF even though every committed blob is already
# LF-only (confirmed: `git show HEAD:<path> | grep -c $'\r'` returns 0 for
# every sampled file type -- .ts/.md/.rs/.json/.html/.gitignore). This was
# the root cause of ~330 of ~365 clean-checkout test failures the review
# found: structural-guard tests whose regexes assume a bare `\n` (e.g.
# `/(^|\n)\/pkg\/(\n|$)/`) never match text that was silently rewritten to
# `\r\n` at checkout time. Adding this file changes NOTHING about the
# already-LF committed blobs -- it only pins the WORKING-TREE CHECKOUT to
# LF regardless of a contributor's own local `core.autocrlf` setting, so
# no repository-wide renormalization commit is needed or included here.
#
# This repository has no tracked binary files and no tracked
# Windows-native script files (.bat/.cmd/.ps1) as of this Arc (confirmed:
# `git ls-files` inventory, Alpha 8121-8200's own reconciliation report) --
# a single blanket rule is therefore the narrowest correct policy. If a
# genuine binary or Windows-native-CRLF-required file is ever added, give
# it its own more specific line ABOVE this one (`git-attributes` uses
# last-match-wins per path).
* text=auto eol=lf
